  "narrRiskFlag": "Risk Flag",
  "narrBelowHurdle": "Below Quality Hurdle",
  "narrStrongLowVal": "Strong Quality, Lower Valuation",
  "narrStrongHighVal": "Strong Quality, High Valuation",
  "narrStrongQuality": "Strong Quality",
  "narrMixed": "Mixed Profile",
  "narrNotScored": "Not Scored",
  "narrBandExcellent": "Score Band: Excellent",
  "narrBandStrong": "Score Band: Strong",
  "narrBandAverage": "Score Band: Average",
  "narrBandWeak": "Score Band: Weak",
  "commonAnd": "and",
  "narrUpdates": "Quarterly results update return on capital, debt, cash flow and growth; daily closing prices update valuation and the 12-month return rank.",
  "mWhatTitle": "What the score is",
  "mWhatBody": "A 0-100 score built only from published numbers: return on capital, debt, cash flow, growth, valuation and the 12-month price return. The same rules apply to every stock, and no person picks or adjusts a score. It describes a company's financial profile; it is not a forecast and not a buy or sell call.",
  "mBands": "Score bands",
  "mBandExcellent": "Excellent: strong on most measures",
  "mBandStrong": "Strong",
  "mBandAverage": "Average",
  "mBandWeak": "Weak: below the quality hurdle, or a risk flag",
  "mPillars": "Three pillars",
  "mPillarsBody": "The overall score is a weighted mix. If valuation or momentum has no data it is left out and its weight is shared by the others; it is never filled with a guessed value.",
  "mQualityBody": "Return on capital (ROCE) 40, debt to equity 25, operating cash flow vs profit 15, 5-year sales and profit growth 20 (full marks at 20% a year sales and 25% profit; shrinking scores 0). ROCE and debt count half on a fixed scale and half on the rank among companies in the same industry (15 or more), else the same sector.",
  "mValuationBody": "P/E compared with companies in the same industry 50, P/E compared with its own 5-year average 30 (0.6x or lower full marks, 0.85x half, 1.3x or higher none), and P/E against 5-year profit growth (PEG) 20 (1 or lower full marks, 3 or higher none; growth counted between 5% and 40% a year). A part with no data is left out. A loss-making company scores 0. Companies that demerged a large business, or have no 5-year average, use the earnings yield vs the 10-year government bond instead of their own average. Banks and NBFCs use P/B: rank within banks or NBFCs 60, against their own 5-year average 40.",
  "mMomentumBody": "Price return over the last 12 months, leaving out the latest month, ranked against every scored stock (6 months for stocks listed under a year). RSI, MACD and moving averages are shown for information and are not scored.",
  "mHurdleBody": "When the quality pillar is below 55, the overall score is capped at 54. From quality 55 to 65 the cap rises step by step (about 4.6 points per quality point) and disappears at 65, so a small change in quality never makes the score jump. A cheap stock or a strong price run cannot lift a weak business into the strong bands.",
  "mMinData": "Minimum data",
  "mMinDataBody": "Quality needs at least 3 of its 4 inputs (return on capital, debt, cash flow, growth). With 2 inputs the overall score is capped at 60; with fewer, or without return on capital, no score is shown and the stock reads DATA PENDING. Missing inputs are never assumed.",
  "mRiskFlags": "Risk flags",
  "mRiskBody": "Any of these caps the score at 28 and shows HIGH RISK FLAG, whatever the other numbers say:",
  "mPledge": "Pledge",
  "mPledgeBody": "75% or more of promoter shares pledged, or pledged shares at 25% or more of the company",
  "mNetWorth": "Net worth",
  "mNetWorthBody": "Zero or negative shareholder equity (held for review instead when the price-to-book in the fundamentals dataset is positive)",
  "mDebt": "Debt",
  "mDebtBody": "A negative debt-to-equity figure (a data anomaly)",
  "mReviewed": "Reviewed pledges",
  "mReviewedBody": "Some large pledges are checked against exchange filings. When the promoter is a private-equity owner that pledged its stake for its own holding-company loan, the pledge is shown as a note and does not trigger the flag. Every other pledge follows the rule above.",
  "mSpecial": "Special cases",
  "mBanks": "Banks and NBFCs",
  "mBanksBody": "Quality is return on equity 30, return on assets 25, net interest margin 15 (banks only), leverage 10 and growth 20. Loan quality (NPA) is not assessed yet, so the score is capped at 75 and shows a \"provisional\" badge.",
  "mBrokers": "Brokers",
  "mBrokersBody": "Debt is not scored (margin funding borrowings); capped at 75 with a \"provisional\" badge.",
  "mInsurance": "Insurance, holding companies, REITs / InvITs",
  "mInsuranceBody": "No score. Their accounts do not fit these ratios; they need embedded value, NAV or yield instead.",
  "mEtfsBody": "Valuation is set to a neutral 60.",
  "mReview": "Data under review",
  "mReviewBody": "No score when our stored fundamentals fail a check against exchange data (market cap or price of a different company). It returns once the data is corrected.",
  "mLabels": "Labels",
  "mPositiveTrend": "Positive trend",
  "mPositiveBody": "Momentum rank 50+. A stock already on the positive side keeps it until the rank falls below 45; one on the weak side needs 55 to cross, so a label does not flip on small daily moves.",
  "mHighStrength": "Quality 70+, valuation 65+, positive trend",
  "mConsolidation": "Quality 70+, valuation 65+, weak trend",
  "mFair": "Quality 70+, valuation 35-64",
  "mExtended": "Quality 70+, valuation below 35, positive trend",
  "mElevated": "Quality 70+, valuation below 35, weak trend",
  "mNeutral": "Quality 55-69",
  "mBelow": "Quality below 55",
  "mNegative": "Quality 70+, but the company is loss-making",
  "mUnavailable": "Quality 70+, but under 6 months of price history or no valuation data",
  "mUnconfirmed": "Pledge data is missing, so the risk check could not run",
  "mDataPending": "Not enough data to score yet",
  "mFreshness": "Data and freshness",
  "mFreshnessBody": "Fundamentals come from a dataset compiled from companies' published results; where a figure is missing, debt and cash flow are taken from Yahoo Finance; net worth, margins and bank balance-sheet figures come from Yahoo Finance. Closing prices come from the NSE daily bhavcopy; prices during market hours come from Yahoo Finance and can be delayed. Scores are recalculated after each trading day's close. Data can be incomplete or wrong; check the company's filings before relying on any number.",
